# Two squirt guns, one frame apart. `movies/level29-990b.zmv` staggered this
# creature 121 times and `d990b_stagger_already` read zero every time; the round
# that ported `$81:96E4` left that as an input problem and guessed at the rhythm
# — *"a burst that stops on fourteen and resumes has not been tried."*
#
# **The guess was the wrong shape, and one measurement says why: the gun fires
# every twelve frames and the flash lasts two.** On `movies/level29-990b.zmv`
# the creature's stagger meter at `$7E:024A` steps down at 3665, 3677, 3689,
# 3701, 3713 — twelve apart, thirty-six when a shot misses, never anything else
# — and its record's `ACTOR_ATTR_SET` goes up on the hit frame and comes back
# down two frames later:
#
#     watch $7E:1AA2  frame  3665  $8011      <- hit, and flashing
#     watch $7E:1AA2  frame  3667  $8001      <- and not, two frames on
#
# So no rhythm one player can play reaches the site. Holding the button down is
# *already* the fastest the gun goes; every burst is slower, and a hit that
# lands ten frames outside the flash and a hit that lands thirty do the same
# nothing. `d990b_stagger_already` does not want timing from one player. It
# wants a **second** one, one frame out of phase.
#
# ## The route is `movies/level29-990b.zmv`'s, given to both ports verbatim
#
# Port 2 presses Start in the player-select window and is then handed the same
# twenty-six route lines, frame for frame. That works because of something worth
# keeping: **two players walking the same input converge.** They enter the level
# 23 pixels apart and are within one pixel of each other by frame 2700, because
# the level 29 chicane is narrow enough that both are held against the same
# walls:
#
#     frame 2580   p1 277,1435   p2 300,1435
#     frame 2700   p1 455,1451   p2 456,1451
#     frame 3600   p1 919,769    p2 926,775
#
# Only the last line differs, and only by one frame:
#
#     3624   Down+Y
#     2:3625 Down+Y
#
# That is the whole input. Both turn round on the `$81:990B` creature that has
# followed them up the level, and neither moves again.
#
# ## What one frame of skew does to the meter
#
# Hits now arrive in pairs a frame apart instead of singly every twelve, so the
# pool empties on the second of a pair while the first is still flashing:
#
#     watch $7E:054A  frame  3740  $0003
#     watch $7E:054A  frame  3741  $0002
#     watch $7E:054A  frame  3742  $0001
#     watch $7E:054A  frame  3743  $0000
#     watch $7E:054A  frame  3744  $FFFF      <- emptied, one frame behind
#
# `d990b_stagger_already` fires 13 times over the run. (The creature is on page
# `$0500` here rather than `$0200`: a second player shifts the thread slots, so
# a watch address copied from the one-player movie reads somebody else.)
#
# ## And it kills it, which was the other open site
#
# `d990b_died` was written down as wanting "a weapon this level has not been
# shown to place", off arithmetic that is exact: the squirt gun's damage-table
# entry is 1, the creature's `$2A` starts at `$0097` — 151 — and a player starts
# level 29 with `$7E:1CCC = $0150`, 150 rounds. **One short, and the cheapest
# answer to being one round short is a second identical gun.** Two players bring
# 300 rounds to 151 health. It dies at frame 4839, and the movie ends 61 frames
# later.
#
# (The level does place bigger guns — see `docs/cosim.md`, which corrects that
# entry: it was read off record 29's object list and this level is record 30.
# Slot 5, twenty damage, is at (351,540) on open ground. This movie does not go
# there, because a second player is 26 route lines of copy-paste and that detour
# is 576 frames.)
#
# 322,347 calls checked, 0 diverged, nothing declined — and two sites that no
# input in forty-seven movies had reached.
#
# Retune by watching the meter and the health:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 4900 -m movies\level29-990b-2p.zmv --watch 054a,3600,4900,1
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 4900 -m movies\level29-990b-2p.zmv --watch 052a,3600,4900,1
